			<div class="content" id="post-content-1869230">
									

<p>This is ludicrous in the best possible ways. I've always adored the idea that, despite all of their resources, the Foundation is constantly overlooking something incredibly fundamental about the things they contain, which is why they grasp so desperately to whatever works regardless of how insane it is. Sometimes that insanity looks like 110-Montauk, and sometimes it looks like <em>this</em>.</p>
<p>The best part, per my headcanon, is that if the Foundation would just bite the bullet and hire a few competent Serpent's Hand types as consultants to look this over, most of it would prove <em>monstrously unnecessary</em>. I picture a conversation something along the lines of, &quot;You know you could just have the little girl throw a drop of squirrel milk over her shoulder and do away with the rest of this right?&quot;</p>
<p>In any case, +1.</p>

